{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":2468433,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,5]],"date-time":"2026-05-05T12:12:48Z","timestamp":1777983168048,"version":"3.51.4"},"description":"Supplemental Information for 10.1021\/acs.jcim.5c03005","reference-count":0,"publisher":"American Chemical Society (ACS)","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.1021\/acs.jcim.5c03005.s001","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,26]],"date-time":"2026-02-26T20:20:50Z","timestamp":1772137250000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["VFMol: A Discrete Flow Matching Variational Autoencoder for Molecular Graph Generation"],"prefix":"10.1021","member":"316","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,23]],"date-time":"2026-03-23T07:31:51Z","timestamp":1774251111000},"score":32.67976,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.acs.org\/doi\/suppl\/10.1021\/acs.jcim.5c03005\/suppl_file\/ci5c03005_si_001.pdf"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1021\/acs.jcim.5c03005.s001","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.1021\/acs.jcim.5c03005","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,14]],"date-time":"2026-05-14T11:16:32Z","timestamp":1778757392998,"version":"3.51.4"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,5]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"American Chemical Society (ACS)","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>We propose ChemMambaFlow, a unified framework that integrates a graphenhanced Mamba encoder with latent flow matching for chemical molecular property prediction and conformation generation. The Graph-Enhanced Mamba Encoder combines graph attention mechanisms with selective state space modeling to capture both local and long-range atomic dependencies. The Latent Flow Matching Conformation Generator efficiently produces 3D molecular structures from SMILES representations through learned probability paths in latent space. A Contribution-Aware Multi-Modal Fusion Module dynamically balances molecular graph and spectroscopic features based on their estimated task contributions. Experiments on MoleculeNet, QM9, and ChemSpectra datasets demonstrate that ChemMambaFlow consistently outperforms existing methods, achieving 88.1% AUROC on HIV, 0.423 RMSE on ESOL, and 0.0176 MAE on QM9, while generating chemically plausible conformations rated 4.43\/5 by expert evaluation.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.26434\/chemrxiv.15002769\/v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,6]],"date-time":"2026-05-06T06:01:51Z","timestamp":1778047311000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["ChemMambaFlow: Graph-Enhanced Mamba with Latent Flow Matching for Molecular Property Prediction and Conformation Generation"],"prefix":"10.26434","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0004-8390-8942","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Zixuan","family":"Shi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Mengyao","family":"Qian","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"316","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/chemrxiv.org\/doi\/pdf\/10.26434\/chemrxiv.15002769\/v1","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,14]],"date-time":"2026-05-14T10:24:52Z","timestamp":1778754292000},"score":30.006336,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/chemrxiv.org\/doi\/full\/10.26434\/chemrxiv.15002769\/v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,5]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.26434\/chemrxiv.15002769\/v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,5]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,16]],"date-time":"2025-10-16T06:59:39Z","timestamp":1760597979605,"version":"3.28.0"},"reference-count":30,"publisher":"IEEE","